// TODO: stale `Call.isKnownUnsaturatedCall` (a lazy val) after eta expansion.
// Only observable once a block simplifier runs before the fused pass: that simplifier inlines `c` into
// `set tmp = p(true); return tmp()`, and in doing so caches `isKnownUnsaturatedCall = false` on the call
// `p(true)`, as `p` has only one parameter list then. Eta expansion adds a second parameter list to `p` but keeps
// that call node, so later simplifiers never combine the two calls into the saturated `p_N$p$worker(true)` below.
// Currently without a block simplifier runs before the fused pass the program gets optimized fine.
// Fix:
// 1. make the fused pass rebuild calls to eta expanded functions (any pass that changes a definition's param lists
//    has to rebuild every call to it.),
// 2. or turn the lazy val `isKnownUnsaturatedCall` into a `def`, since it depends on the mutable
//    `irDefn` of the callee symbol (enough for this example; unsure whether the lazy val `isPure`, which is computed
//    from `isKnownUnsaturatedCall`, also needs to become a `def`).
:expect 1
:soir
@noInline fun p(b) = if b then A else B
fun c(x) = if x is
  A then 1
  B then 2
c(p(true))
//│ deforest > >>> fusing >>>
//│ deforest > A⁰ ->
//│ deforest > 	match: x²
//│ deforest > B⁰ ->
//│ deforest > 	match: x²
//│ deforest > <<< fusing <<<
//│ eta-expansion > >>> eta-expansion targets shapes >>>
//│ eta-expansion > p_7$p: [1, 0]
//│ eta-expansion > <<< eta-expansion targets shapes <<<
//│ dead-param-elim > >>> dead-param-elim results >>>
//│ dead-param-elim > <<< dead-param-elim results <<<
